    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core led by **Yordan Alvarez** (76.89) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (74.82). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier offensive engine, buoyed by a 0.450 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Tanner Bibee, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns top-tier marks due to his explosive speed profile; facing a pitcher with a slow delivery, his ability to manufacture SBs makes him a massive value add for our 5x5 Roto standing. **Junior Caminero** (69.42) also secures a premium spot in the lineup, benefiting from a soft matchup against Poulin (5.00 xERA) which compensates for a marginal park factor. These plays are bolstered by significant platoon advantages, particularly for **Josh Smith** (64.66) and **Lars Nootbaar** (63.95), both of whom see their projections climb significantly due to strong handedness splits against their respective right-handed opponents.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Casey Schmitt**, whose 41.80 score fell just short of the threshold for a start. While **Casey Schmitt** offers a respectable platoon edge against Bachar, he lacked the volume of upside compared to our mid-tier starters like **Nelson Velazquez** (55.26), who retains a higher raw projection despite the slight penalty for a right-on-right matchup. We are closely monitoring the status of **Christian Yelich**, who holds a solid 58.43 rating despite a negative platoon shift; we are banking on his leadoff positioning and high base efficiency to anchor the top of the order. Investors should note that a significant portion of the roster\u2014including **Gary Sanchez**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Josh Smith**, **Christian Yelich**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Nelson Velazquez**\u2014is pending official lineup confirmation. Any shift down the order for these players could impact their efficiency, though we remain confident in their ability to outperform their floor in favorable matchups.",
